WHAT THIS COVERS
----------------
`LICENSE` (MIT) speaks about the Software. It says nothing about a database
right, which leaves the data in this repository -- the part a reader is most
likely to reuse -- with unstated terms. This file states them, by path:

    reference/**                    published values, transcribed capacities,
                                    and the reconstructed transition matrix
    data/raw/precips_c0_*.csv       the committed precipitation scenarios
    results/clean/**                the cleaned output
    artifacts/**                    the frozen instances and their solutions
    results/*.csv                   the reproduced tables
    figures/**                      the published result figures

Everything else, including all Python source and the archived originals
under `archive/`, is covered by `LICENSE` (MIT).

